      "widgets_values": [
        "# FLUX.2 Klein 9B \u2014 instruction edit\n\n## How to use it\n\n1. Load your image on **Source image**.\n2. Type what you want changed in **Instruction**, in plain English.\n3. Queue.\n\nThat is the whole workflow. There is no mask, no crop, no denoise slider.\n\n## Why this model and not Krea 2 Turbo\n\n`krea2TurboFP8_krea2TURBO` is a **text-to-image** model. It has no socket that\naccepts an image \u2014 the only way to give it a picture is to hand it a noisy latent\n(`denoise < 1.0`, which regenerates everything) or to fence off a region with a\nmask. Neither is \"look at this and do what I say\".\n\nFLUX.2 is an **edit model**. `ReferenceLatent` splices the encoded source image\ndirectly into the conditioning, so the transformer attends to your photo and your\nsentence at the same time and returns the photo with the change applied.\n`ReferenceLatent` lives in ComfyUI's `nodes_edit_model.py`; that is the whole\ndistinction in one node.\n\n## The matched set \u2014 change one, change all of them\n\n| slot | value |\n|---|---|\n| diffusion model | `flux-2-klein-9b-fp8.safetensors` (distilled) |\n| text encoder | `qwen_3_8b_fp8mixed.safetensors` \u2014 `CLIPLoader type = **flux2**` |\n| VAE | `flux2-vae.safetensors` |\n| latent | `EmptyFlux2LatentImage` \u2014 **128-channel**, nothing else emits it |\n| patch node | **none** \u2014 no `ModelSampling*`, no `FluxGuidance` |\n| sampling | `RandomNoise \u2192 CFGGuider \u2192 SamplerCustomAdvanced`, sigmas from `Flux2Scheduler` |\n\n**Distilled \u21d2 `CFGGuider.cfg = 1.0` and 4 steps.** The negative branch is not\nevaluated at CFG 1.0, which is why it is a `ConditioningZeroOut` and not a\nprompt. If you ever swap in the *base* 9B (not on this box) it becomes 20 steps\nat CFG 5.0 with a real empty `CLIPTextEncode` for the negative.\n\n## Writing the instruction\n\nIt is an **instruction**, not a caption. Describe the change, not the picture.\n\n- \u2705 `Add a black silk top hat to the dog's head.`\n- \u2705 `Put a red bow tie on the dog and leave everything else unchanged.`\n- \u274c `a dog wearing a top hat, photorealistic, 8k, sharp` \u2014 that is t2i prompting\n  and it pushes the model to regenerate the whole frame.\n\nNaming what must stay fixed genuinely helps: *\"...keep the background, the pose\nand the lighting exactly as they are.\"*\n\n## Knobs, in the order worth touching\n\n1. **`noise_seed`** on Random noise \u2014 a 4-step distilled model is seed-sensitive.\n   Re-roll before you change anything else.\n2. **`steps`** on Flux2 scheduler \u2014 4 is the distilled default. 6\u20138 sometimes\n   cleans up a fiddly edit at proportional cost.\n3. **`megapixels`** on Fit to ~1 MP \u2014 the model's native working area. Raising it\n   costs time and tends to *reduce* instruction adherence.\n\n`resolution_steps = 16` snaps the resized image to a multiple of 16, which is\nwhat the 128-channel latent wants (H/16 \u00d7 W/16). The stock template ships `1`;\n16 avoids an off-by-a-few-pixels resize on odd input aspect ratios.\n\n## LoRAs \u2014 where they go\n\n**Between `UNETLoader` and `CFGGuider.model`.** That is the entire answer: in\nthis graph `MODEL` is touched exactly once, on the single wire from the loader to\nthe guider, so the LoRA slot is the only thing that can sit on it.\n\n```\nUNETLoader \u2500\u2500> LoraLoaderModelOnly \u2500\u2500> CFGGuider.model\n```\n\nThe slot is already in the graph, **bypassed** (`Mode: Never/Bypass`, the purple\nnode). Right-click it \u2192 **Mode \u2192 Always** to switch it on. Bypass re-points the\nMODEL output to the MODEL input, so while it is off the model flows past\nuntouched \u2014 no need to delete or rewire anything.\n\n### Use `LoraLoaderModelOnly`, not `LoraLoader`\n\n`V4_flux_klein.safetensors` contains 224 tensors and **every one of them is\n`diffusion_model.*`**. There are no text-encoder keys, so the CLIP half of a\nregular `LoraLoader` would be a no-op taking up two sockets. Model-only is the\nhonest wiring. (If you ever get a FLUX.2 LoRA that *does* carry text-encoder\nweights, swap in `LoraLoader` and route `CLIPLoader \u2192 lora.clip \u2192\nCLIPTextEncode.clip` \u2014 one CLIP wire, patched once, upstream of both\n`ReferenceLatent` branches.)\n\n### Stacking more than one\n\nChain them. Each takes MODEL and returns MODEL:\n\n```\nUNETLoader \u2500\u2500> LoraLoaderModelOnly(A) \u2500\u2500> LoraLoaderModelOnly(B) \u2500\u2500> CFGGuider.model\n```\n\nOrder changes the result slightly (the patches compose non-commutatively) but\nrarely enough to matter. `Power Lora Loader (rgthree)` is installed if you want\nseveral in one node with individual toggles.\n\n### A wrong-family LoRA does not error\n\nIt logs a wall of `lora key not loaded` to the console and completes with **zero\neffect**. If a LoRA \"does nothing\", read the console before touching strength.\nOf the 12 LoRAs on this box, exactly **one** is FLUX.2 Klein:\n\n| LoRA | Family | Works here |\n|---|---|---|\n| `V4_flux_klein.safetensors` | `flux2_klein_9b` \u2014 112/112 keys matched | \u2705 |\n| `CYPERPUNK_KREA_2`, `MysticXXX_KREA2_*`, `krea2_turbo_*` | Krea 2 | \u274c |\n| `zit_oilpainting`, `zit_watercolor` | Z-Image | \u274c |\n| `chroma-flash-heun_r32` | Chroma (FLUX.1 Schnell derivative) | \u274c |\n| `sdxl_oil painting` | SDXL | \u274c |\n| `Wan21_I2V_*`, `wan2.1_SCAIL_2_DPO` | Wan 2.1 | \u274c |\n\n**`V4_flux_klein` has a trigger word: `fluxtrait`.** Its metadata says\n`ss_tag_frequency: {\"1_fluxtrait\": {\"fluxtrait\": 1}}` \u2014 it was trained on a\nsingle concept under that token. Put the word in the instruction or the LoRA\nwill be much weaker than its strength setting suggests.\n\n### Strength, and the distillation caveat\n\n`strength_model` 1.0 is the trained default; 0.6\u20130.8 is the usual dial-back for\na style LoRA that is overpowering the edit. Negative values invert it.\n\nWorth knowing: this Klein is the **distilled** 4-step checkpoint. A LoRA trained\nagainst the *base* model is fighting the distillation, and the usual symptom is\nmush at 4 steps that cleans up at 8. If a LoRA looks broken, raise\n`Flux2Scheduler.steps` before you conclude it is incompatible.\n\n## Output size follows the input\n\n`GetImageSize` reads the resized source and drives **both** `Flux2Scheduler` and\n`EmptyFlux2LatentImage`. So the result comes back at your image's aspect ratio\nautomatically \u2014 the `width`/`height` widgets on those two nodes are overridden by\nthe wire and are only defaults.\n"
      ],
